An efficient and standard way to solve this problem is to work in **reverse**. 

When bricks are removed, connected components break apart, which is hard to maintain dynamically. However, if we process the hits in reverse order, removing a brick becomes **adding** a brick, which allows us to use a **Disjoint Set Union (DSU)** data structure.

### Algorithm
1. Mark all the hit cells in the grid by decrementing their values (`grid[r][c]--`). Bricks that were originally `1` will become `0` (or `< 0` if an empty cell was hit).
2. Construct a DSU over all cells plus a virtual "roof" node (`0`):
   - Union every remaining brick (`grid[r][c] == 1`) with its adjacent remaining bricks.
   - For any brick in the top row (`r == 0`), union it with the roof.
3. Process the queries in reverse from `hits.length - 1` down to `0`:
   - For each hit `(r, c)`, restore the cell: `grid[r][c]++`.
   - If the cell was not originally a brick (`grid[r][c] != 1`), `0` bricks fall.
   - Otherwise, record the size of the component connected to the roof before adding this brick.
   - If `r == 0`, connect the brick to the roof.
   - Union this brick with all its adjacent existing bricks.
   - If the newly added brick is connected to the roof, the number of bricks that fell due to its removal is:
     $$\max(0, \text{roof\_size\_after} - \text{roof\_size\_before} - 1)$$
     (subtracting `1` because the hit brick itself was erased, not fallen).
4. Return the resulting counts.

### Java Solution

```java
class Solution {
    private static class DSU {
        int[] parent;
        int[] size;

        DSU(int n) {
            parent = new int[n];
            size = new int[n];
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                parent[i] = i;
                size[i] = 1;
            }
        }

        int find(int i) {
            if (parent[i] == i)
                return i;
            return parent[i] = find(parent[i]);
        }

        void union(int i, int j) {
            int rootI = find(i);
            int rootJ = find(j);
            if (rootI != rootJ) {
                parent[rootI] = rootJ;
                size[rootJ] += size[rootI];
            }
        }

        int getSize(int i) {
            return size[find(i)];
        }
    }

    public int[] hitBricks(int[][] grid, int[][] hits) {
        int m = grid.length;
        int n = grid[0].length;

        // Mark all hits
        for (int[] hit : hits) {
            grid[hit[0]][hit[1]]--;
        }

        // Virtual roof node is at index 0. Grid cells are mapped to 1 .. m * n.
        DSU dsu = new DSU(m * n + 1);

        int[][] dirs = {{-1, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, -1}, {0, 1}};

        // Build the initial graph with remaining bricks
        for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {
                if (grid[r][c] == 1) {
                    int node = r * n + c + 1;
                    if (r == 0) {
                        dsu.union(node, 0);
                    }
                    for (int[] d : dirs) {
                        int nr = r + d[0];
                        int nc = c + d[1];
                        if (nr >= 0 && nr < m && nc >= 0 && nc < n && grid[nr][nc] == 1) {
                            dsu.union(node, nr * n + nc + 1);
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        int[] result = new int[hits.length];

        // Process hits in reverse
        for (int i = hits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            int r = hits[i][0];
            int c = hits[i][1];

            grid[r][c]++;
            if (grid[r][c] == 1) {
                int node = r * n + c + 1;
                int prevRoofSize = dsu.getSize(0);

                if (r == 0) {
                    dsu.union(node, 0);
                }

                for (int[] d : dirs) {
                    int nr = r + d[0];
                    int nc = c + d[1];
                    if (nr >= 0 && nr < m && nc >= 0 && nc < n && grid[nr][nc] == 1) {
                        dsu.union(node, nr * n + nc + 1);
                    }
                }

                int currRoofSize = dsu.getSize(0);
                // If the restored brick is connected to the roof, calculate newly attached bricks
                if (dsu.find(node) == dsu.find(0)) {
                    result[i] = Math.max(0, currRoofSize - prevRoofSize - 1);
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
