An efficient and clean solution in Java to solve the **Remove Invalid Parentheses** problem.

### Method Explanation

1. **Count Removals**: 
   First, we determine the minimum number of misplaced left (`remL`) and right (`remR`) parentheses that must be removed. 
   - A single pass over the string updates `remL` and `remR`.
2. **Backtracking (DFS)**:
   - We perform a backtracking depth-first search starting from index 0.
   - At each character:
     - If it is `'('`, we can either remove it (if `remL > 0`) or keep it (incrementing open parenthesis count `open`).
     - If it is `')'`, we can either remove it (if `remR > 0`) or keep it (decrementing `open`, provided `open > 0`).
     - If it is any other character, we simply keep it.
   - At the end of the string, if `remL == 0`, `remR == 0`, and `open == 0`, the constructed string is valid and we add it to a `Set` to ensure uniqueness.

Given that there are at most 20 parentheses, pruning invalid paths with `open < 0`, `remL < 0`, and `remR < 0` keeps the search space very small and well within the time limit.

### Java Source Code

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public List<String> removeInvalidParentheses(String s) {
        int remL = 0, remR = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            char c = s.charAt(i);
            if (c == '(') {
                remL++;
            } else if (c == ')') {
                if (remL > 0) {
                    remL--;
                } else {
                    remR++;
                }
            }
        }

        Set<String> result = new HashSet<>();
        dfs(s, 0, remL, remR, 0, new StringBuilder(), result);
        return new ArrayList<>(result);
    }

    private void dfs(String s, int index, int remL, int remR, int open, StringBuilder sb, Set<String> result) {
        if (remL < 0 || remR < 0 || open < 0) {
            return;
        }

        if (index == s.length()) {
            if (remL == 0 && remR == 0 && open == 0) {
                result.add(sb.toString());
            }
            return;
        }

        char c = s.charAt(index);
        int len = sb.length();

        if (c == '(') {
            // Option 1: Remove '('
            dfs(s, index + 1, remL - 1, remR, open, sb, result);
            // Option 2: Keep '('
            sb.append(c);
            dfs(s, index + 1, remL, remR, open + 1, sb, result);
            sb.setLength(len);
        } else if (c == ')') {
            // Option 1: Remove ')'
            dfs(s, index + 1, remL, remR - 1, open, sb, result);
            // Option 2: Keep ')'
            sb.append(c);
            dfs(s, index + 1, remL, remR, open - 1, sb, result);
            sb.setLength(len);
        } else {
            // Non-parenthesis characters are always kept
            sb.append(c);
            dfs(s, index + 1, remL, remR, open, sb, result);
            sb.setLength(len);
        }
    }
}
